MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The resistor assortment fits my breadboard, LED, and PCB purchases because it supplies useful parts for experimenting with circuits.",
    "The digital caliper would help me check board dimensions, component spacing, and hardware fit across my DIY projects. Circuit-testing tools also fit my electronics interests, although I would need a specific task before choosing them."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The filament and acrylic cement assume projects I have not shown a need for; building circuits does not mean I currently print parts or assemble acrylic.",
    "The thermal camera does not address a clear gap in my current temperature checks, which my infrared thermometer already covers."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in DIY projects seems to have been stretched into a need for unrelated fabrication supplies.",
    "An interest in circuit troubleshooting seems to have been treated as enough reason to suggest an oscilloscope and its accessories, even though my equipment ownership and compatibility needs are unclear."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I am more likely to choose something with an immediate use, such as resistors for circuit experiments or a caliper for checking fit, than equipment whose purpose depends on a future project.",
    "My existing supplies matter: the PCB assortment already included switches, so another switch kit is less compelling until I check what remains. Small circuit connections also matter more to me than large alligator clips."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my practical electronics interests but assumed too many additional projects and equipment needs."
}
